  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health Resilience of Northeast Nigeria (HeRON)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To note that the primary donor for this follow-on project is USAID. FCDO has made a 2million GBP contribution to the overall 15,586,960 USD project. This record only shows the transactions related to the FCDO portion of the funds, as per section A.5 of the Cooperative Agreement with USAID.

Two year continuation of the existing Heron contract (DF221) implemented by USAID and FCDO. The project will be implemented in consortium with AAH and SFH (IRC is the PRIME). Activities will focus on health, nutrition, WASH and governance with a focus on system strengthening. Total award includes $5m contingency funds which may or may not be activated to respond in Adamawa -- if yes IRC will develop separate budget for it.</narrative>
  </description>
